{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfrzsS7h2DiCMAtbBrFs9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `metrics/counter.py`, and `tests/test_metrics.py` passed on all 5 runs in a row. I didn't add a test for `snapshot()`, so the mid-update fix is untested.\n\n**Cause:** `incr` read the value, yielded, then wrote it back with no lock, so concurrent increments overwrote each other. `snapshot()` copied the dict while other threads were mutating it.\n\n**Fix:**\n- **Per-name locks:** each counter name has its own cell holding a value and a `threading.Lock`. `incr` locks only its own cell, so different counters don't block each other.\n- **Registry lock:** a separate lock guards only the name-to-cell mapping and is held just long enough to look up or create a cell. `incr` never holds it together with a cell lock.\n- **`snapshot()`:** it takes the registry lock, then every cell lock, and builds a plain `dict`. The copy is a consistent point in time, with no increment half-done. While it runs, increments and new-name creation wait briefly.\n- **API:** `incr`, `get`, `snapshot` and `reset` keep their signatures. `reset` still removes the key, so a reset name no longer appears in `snapshot()`.\n- **`reset` edge case:** an `incr` that grabbed a cell just before `reset` removed it lands on the discarded cell. That behaves as if the increment happened before the reset."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11263,"cache_read_input_tokens":30405,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11263},"output_tokens":461,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c4892ca-95a5-4c56-ade8-7df88d397e0b","uuid":"5c8799fd-cec7-4e0a-9b8f-357dac3d88e2","timestamp":"2026-10-09T